  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03CC">Definition <span data-tag="03CC">7.14.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}_ i$, $i = 1, 2, 3$ be sites. Let $f : \mathcal{C}_1 \to \mathcal{C}_2$ and $g : \mathcal{C}_2 \to \mathcal{C}_3$ be morphisms of sites given by continuous functors $u : \mathcal{C}_2 \to \mathcal{C}_1$ and $v : \mathcal{C}_3 \to \mathcal{C}_2$. The <em>composition</em> $g \circ f$ is the morphism of sites corresponding to the functor $u \circ v$. </p>
